<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syngman Rhee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1875">1875</a>–<a href="/years/1965">1965</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Rhee Syng-man</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syngman Rhee was a Korean independence activist and the first President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, from 1948 to 1960. He was the first president of the Korean Provisional Government in exile in 1919, spent decades in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and returned in 1945 with American support. His authoritarian rule ended when the April Revolution of 1960 forced him into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/syngman-rhee.jpg" alt="Syngman Rhee" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhee_Syng-Man_in_1948.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
